In Table \ref{tab:CTR-GCN-2D}, when using CTR-GCN as the backbone in the MixGCN branch, we present the recognition accuracy of four skeleton modalities in UAV-Human dataset. Meanwhile, in Table \ref{tab:CTR-GCN-3D}, we demonstrate the accuracy of estimating 3D poses from 2D poses using MotionBert and utilizing these 3D poses for action recognition. In addition, in Table \ref{tab:TD-GCN-2D} and Table \ref{tab:MST-GCN-2D}, we also report the recognition accuracy of using TD-GCN and MST-GCN to model 2D skeleton modalities. Finally, in Table \ref{tab:Mixformer-2D}, we present the recognition accuracy when using Skeleton MixFormer as the backbone in the MixFormer branch.

