\section{Conclusions}
We propose a novel dual-branch framework called Hybrid Dual-branch Network (HDBN) for robust skeleton-based action recognition, which introduces the Transformers and GCNs to model 2D and 3D skeleton data. Different from previous methods using single backbone or using different backbone to process various modalities, our HDBN is to leverage both Transformers and GCNs with the aim of robust skeleton-based action recognition. The effectiveness of HDBN is verified on the UAV-Human dataset, where our HDBN outperforms most existing methods.

